The remember command's --json output was reporting a fact before merge rather than the final persisted state. When re-remembering an existing fact, the JSON output did not reflect the actual merged record stored in Brain—including retained original metadata, appended provenance anchors, and reactivation status changes.
Solution:
Added a line in facts_write_cmd.go that updates the output record to the merged fact after upsert. This ensures --json reports the persisted record, not the pre-merge state. A new test verifies the entire merged result including origin, timestamps, status transitions, kind changes, and provenance chain.", "etag": "W/"2026-09-28T10:06:14.043388Z""}}}

